Sofia, I arrived at the station and immediately saw a bakery.
On Sunday the normal shops are closed.
But in the station the bakeries are always open.
So I went inside.
I bought the bread roll there.
Then I went up to the platform.
The trains run up there on a viaduct.
Up there I waited for the S-Bahn.
After a few minutes the train came.
I quickly got in.
On Sunday morning not many people are out and about yet.
I walked a bit through the carriage.
And I found a nice seat by the window.
I put my rucksack on the seat next to me.
I sat down and looked out of the window.
Then I finally ate the bread roll.
Shortly after that, the S-Bahn set off.
